                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I haven't played this game much yet, and it's still early access. This is less of an in depth review and more of a preview.\n\nThis is Mario Maker as a bullet hell shooter. I like that you have 360 degree shooting instead of just straight forward, but basically this game is a bullet hell shooter where all the levels are made by other people who own the game. How good the game is going to largely rely on the content made by the community.\n\nHowever, the mechanics felt good and the tools are solid. I like the customization for designing levels, and I'm really interested in seeing where the game goes from here. I wish more things were unlocked straight from the beginning, but I wouldn't be surprised to see stuff like that changed.\n\nI also like the art in game, but the portrait art is not my favorite.",
